  "scope_notes": "Modifies Guix package definitions for glibc, adds glibc patches for deterministic store paths and NSS static linking, and modifies post-build ELF validation scripts.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Added a Guix helper generating `-ffile-prefix-map` flags to remap `/gnu/store` directories to `/usr` in CFLAGS and CPPFLAGS when compiling glibc.",
  "card": "Configures Guix to build official Linux x86_64 and aarch64 release binaries (excluding bitcoin-qt) as static position-independent executables (-static-pie) using glibc 2.44. This allows bitcoind and command-line utilities to run on musl-based distributions like Alpine Linux and on older Linux installations without dynamic linker dependencies, and enables aarch64 pointer authentication (#19075). A known trade-off is that dynamic NSS modules (such as mDNS, LDAP, or SSSD) will no longer function for name resolution in bitcoind. Post-build symbol and security checks are adjusted to inspect static ELF executables.",
